= Cell membrane — Simple =

A '''cell membrane''' is a thin, flexible boundary around a cell. It helps separate what is inside from what is outside.

The membrane is mainly made from a double layer of fats called lipids, with different proteins embedded in or attached to it. Some proteins help particular substances enter or leave; others help the cell receive signals.

The membrane is not a sealed wall. It is selective, helping cells maintain conditions needed for life through [[Homeostasis|homeostasis]] and other processes.

